tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-shape.hero:29:46: error[counted_by_shape]: `counted_by` on `p` of `not_a_pointer` names no extent — `counted_by` says how far C reads or writes through a `ptr`, or through a group's record lent whole with `@`, and `p` is neither
tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-shape.hero:30:48: error[counted_by_shape]: `counted_by` on `p` of `no_such_sibling` names no extent — `m` names no other parameter of `no_such_sibling` and no `constant` of its group — the extent is the sibling C reads the count from, a constant the group declares from the header, or the number itself
tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-shape.hero:31:47: error[counted_by_shape]: `counted_by` on `p` of `not_an_integer` names no extent — `n` is not an integer C takes by value or reads through an `@` cell, so it cannot say how far C reads — an extent is `i32`, `u64`, or another width the header spells
tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-shape.hero:37:24: error[field_lend_uncounted]: `.ptr()` lends a field's address to C with an extent this call states, and `p` of `slot_sum` does not say which argument the extent is — so nothing can check the number against the field
